@startuml
title 3.5.6 Evaluate and version a matching model
caption UC-105 | Planned | Proposed design
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: docs/requirements/uc.md
' Main entity migration: Proposed entity; no migration
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Admin" as Actor
participant "Proposed Model Review" as Page
participant "Proposed Matching API" as API
participant "Proposed Training Service" as Service
participant "matching_model_versions" as Table <<proposed entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Evaluate and version a matching model
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: Evaluate and approve model version (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Evaluate and version a matching model
activate Service
Service -> Table: 5: Proposed: load candidate and held-out evaluation metadata
activate Table
Table --> Service: 6: Candidate model version
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 7: Evaluate quality, privacy, regressions and rollback readiness
alt Approved evaluation passes
Service -> Table: 8: Proposed: record explicit approval and version activation
activate Table
Table --> Service: 9: Approved version and rollback reference
deactivate Table
Service --> API: 10: Approved model version
API --> Page: 11: HTTP 200: Approved model version
Page --> Actor: 12: Show authorized result
else Evaluation rejected
Service --> API: 8.1: Keep current matcher; no automatic activation
API --> Page: 8.2: HTTP 409
Page --> Actor: 8.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: Proposed rejection: invalid input / authorization
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Current runtime is rule-v2, not this proposed custom-model lifecycle. Separate policy and
release approval are required.
endlegend
@enduml
